{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense alternatives analyst. You weigh options for a team lead without inventing evidence or clearing review flags.\nYour personal goal is: Compare two or three candidate actions on evidence, applicability and severity fit."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Compare 2-3 materially different candidate actions for this topic. If the draft proposes an action, include it as the incumbent candidate (incumbent true) with its action_type, instruction, draft_text and rationale copied exactly; include NO_ACTION when observing is plausible. For each operational candidate state intervention_need (kind, why intervening now is needed, evidence) and rate need_strength, temporal_scope (does every current claim rest on current, in-scope sources?), proportionality (is the step proportionate to the evidence and impact?) and list unresolved_assumptions. A source need not literally prescribe a recommendation; a clarification or referral is not wrong merely because questions remain. Set decision: KEEP_INCUMBENT, REPLACE_INCUMBENT (prefer a different candidate that is clearly better) or CLOSE_CALL (close_call true; no winner). For each, cite only evidence_ids present in the evidence provided, and rate evidence support, applicability (current versus historical-only sources) and fit with the assessed severity. Do not invent evidence, outcomes or causes. Refer to people by role (a tutor, the team lead), never by name. Write instruction (one concrete sentence telling the team lead what to do), draft_text (the copyable draft) and rationale (why it helps) in plain words, with no evidence IDs or field names. Name a preferred candidate only if it is clearly better; otherwise set close_call true. Your selection does not resolve the review triggers listed; a team lead decides.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_35db244277f41789\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_35db244277f41789/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Conflicting guidance source of truth\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_4339357fd56b8213e42628c8\", \"member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259\"]}, \"draft\": {\"contract_version\": \"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\", \"summary\": \"A QA tutor asks in two threads which source to follow when written guidance appears to conflict. A different QA tutor answered the screenshot question for that case, but the separate question about whether a later announcement replaces an older note remains unanswered in its thread.\", \"summary_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in two threads which source to follow when written guidance appears to conflict.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\"], \"depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"A different QA tutor answered the screenshot question for that case, but the separate question about whether a later announcement replaces an older note remains unanswered in its thread.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c3\", \"c5\"], \"depends_on\": []}], \"detail_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"In the earlier thread, a QA tutor reports that a guide example contradicts the previous Friday’s alignment and asks whether a later announcement replaces an older note.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"In the later thread, a different QA tutor says to follow the thread clarification for that case while the written examples are reconciled, rather than treating the older screenshot as independent authority.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c3\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"The current guidance retrieved for this run does not identify the disputed sources or settle whether one replaces another.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c4\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"The earlier decision records retrieved for this run concern a batch-14 tie-calibration exercise, not the reported source conflict.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c6\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}], \"reasoning\": \"The two questions come from the same QA tutor, not two distinct affected reporters. The later thread has a case-specific answer from a different QA tutor; it is evidence of that answer, not project guidance or a team lead instruction. The earlier supersession question remains unanswered. Follow-up retrieval added scoring guidance, unrelated announcements and batch-14 tie-calibration records, but did not identify the disputed sources or their supersession history. A focused comparison is supported; choosing a governing source or correcting documentation is not yet supported. The two upstream review flags attached to retrieved announcements remain open.\", \"claims\": [{\"claim_id\": \"c1\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that a guide example contradicts the previous Friday’s alignment and asks whether a later announcement replaces an older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c2\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"The same QA tutor asks in a separate thread whether to follow a pinned update or an older scoring-guide screenshot.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c3\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A different QA tutor answers the screenshot question by saying to f